caption: $:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate
title: $:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/docs/api/tags/panel-template

! Summary

Dual-context sections (rendering in BOTH the panel and the new-item modal) live in `ui/attributes/` and carry BOTH tags plus BOTH group tags — the chassis of each context provides `section-target`/`section-type`/`section-mode`, and a single body serves both (write-once, tagged twice). Single-context sections keep `ui/panel/` or `ui/modal/`. Naming revisit-trigger: if a future dual section is not an item attribute, reconsider the `ui/attributes` name.
Add a section to the attributes panel shown on item tiddlers.

! Detail
Tag a tiddler with `$:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate` to make it a panel section. Give it a `caption` field for the section legend. Additionally tag it with a portion tag to place it (untagged members land in Portion/1):

| !Portion tag | !Position |
|$:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate/Portion/Top |Full width above the portions (picker label: "Top, full-width") |
|$:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate/Portion/1 |First (only) portion |
|$:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate/Portion/N |Nth portion — portions sit side by side; a portion exists the moment a section claims it |
|$:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate/Portion/Full |Full width below the portions (picker label: "Bottom, full-width") |

Set portions from the Settings → Panel and modal Portion picker beside each row, or by tag — the picker always offers one number beyond the highest in use, so a new portion is one pick away. The same vocabulary applies to modal sections and dashboard lists.

Sections render inside a `<fieldset>`; gate content with `is[current]` type tags so sections only apply to relevant types:

```
title: $:/plugins/MyPlugin/ui/panel/due-date
caption: Due
tags: $:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate $:/tags/hypergsd/PanelTemplate/Portion/1

<%if [is[current]tag[$:/GSD/Action]] %>
    …section content…
<%endif%>
```

The view's placement (above/below the body) is configurable per type via the [[ViewPlacement|$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/docs/api/tags/view-placement]] tag list (`$:/config/hypergsd/Placement/*`); the orientation within a group (stacked or flowing) is the `$:/config/hypergsd/panel-layout` setting (Panel and modal tab, shared with the modal).

! Best Practice
Interactive controls: standard widgets carry their own handling; raw `<input>`/`<button>` elements only work for the plugin's `data-hgsd-*` actions via the event delegation — new actions require extending the event handler module.